WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:04.302
KATARA: Water.

00:04.886 --> 00:06.429
Earth.

00:06.763 --> 00:08.640
Fire.

00:08.932 --> 00:10.600
Air.

00:11.309 --> 00:14.812
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.355 --> 00:19.359
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.734 --> 00:23.530
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

00:23.738 --> 00:27.158
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.492 --> 00:31.120
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.246 --> 00:32.872
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.997 --> 00:35.208
And although his
airbending skills are great,

00:35.333 --> 00:38.002
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:38.086 --> 00:39.087
AANG: Oof.

00:39.212 --> 00:42.215
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:48.096 --> 00:50.139
NARRATOR: ( READING )

00:50.473 --> 00:53.059
The Avatar has kidnapped my daughter.

00:54.185 --> 00:58.523
I want you to do whatever it takes
to bring her home.

01:02.485 --> 01:03.903
Augh!

01:04.279 --> 01:05.655
Sandbenders, shoo!

01:05.738 --> 01:07.198
Away from the bison!

01:07.615 --> 01:09.200
Library's sinking...

01:09.325 --> 01:10.785
Library's sinking!

01:12.704 --> 01:14.205
( ROARS )

01:17.875 --> 01:19.002
TOPH: No!

01:19.210 --> 01:20.420
I'm sorry, Appa.

01:20.878 --> 01:21.921
Where's Appa?

01:22.589 --> 01:23.715
( GROANS )

01:33.433 --> 01:36.561
( WIND BLOWING )

01:36.644 --> 01:38.563
MOMO: ( PURRING )

01:42.859 --> 01:44.444
How could you let them take Appa?

01:44.611 --> 01:45.820
Why didn't you stop them?

01:46.029 --> 01:47.405
I couldn't!

01:47.488 --> 01:50.283
The library was sinking,
you guys were still inside, and...

01:50.533 --> 01:51.951
You could've come to get us.

01:52.035 --> 01:53.119
I could've saved him!

01:53.202 --> 01:55.204
I can hardly feel any vibrations out here.

01:55.288 --> 01:58.124
The sandbenders snuck up on me,
and there wasn't time for...

01:58.207 --> 01:59.292
You just didn't care!

01:59.375 --> 02:00.501
You never liked Appa!

02:00.585 --> 02:01.711
You wanted him gone.

02:01.919 --> 02:03.046
Aang, stop it.

02:03.129 --> 02:05.340
You know Toph did all she could.

02:05.423 --> 02:06.591
She saved our lives.

02:06.883 --> 02:08.426
Who's gonna save our lives now?

02:08.509 --> 02:10.094
We'll never make it out of here.

02:10.303 --> 02:12.805
That's all any of you guys
care about, yourselves.

02:13.222 --> 02:15.475
You don't care whether
Appa is okay or not.

02:16.100 --> 02:19.354
We're all concerned,
but we can't afford to be fighting, now.

02:20.605 --> 02:22.065
I'm going after Appa.

02:22.357 --> 02:24.359
Aang, wait!

02:26.944 --> 02:28.738
We'd better start walking.

02:28.821 --> 02:31.407
We're the only people who know
about the solar eclipse.

02:31.491 --> 02:33.951
We have to get that information
to Ba Sing Se.

02:35.870 --> 02:39.624
You think if we dig out
the giant owl, he'll give us a ride?

02:43.670 --> 02:46.172
( GROANING )

02:46.798 --> 02:48.257
Maybe we should make camp.

02:48.341 --> 02:51.594
No, please, don't stop just for me.

02:52.553 --> 02:55.014
( MOANING )

02:58.226 --> 03:00.103
( GROANS )

03:01.437 --> 03:03.147
( GRUMBLES )

03:03.648 --> 03:05.191
What now?

03:12.949 --> 03:17.704
Colonel Mongke, what a pleasant surprise.

03:18.204 --> 03:20.540
If you're surprised we're here,

03:20.623 --> 03:23.626
then the Dragon of the West
has lost a few steps.

03:29.882 --> 03:31.759
You know these guys?

03:31.926 --> 03:36.389
Sure, Colonel Mongke
and the Rough Rhinos are legendary.

03:36.723 --> 03:40.852
Each one is a different kind
of weapon specialist.

03:40.977 --> 03:44.313
They are also
a very capable singing group.

03:44.731 --> 03:47.066
We're not here to give a concert!

03:47.150 --> 03:49.193
We're here to apprehend fugitives.

03:49.569 --> 03:51.529
Would you like some tea first?

03:51.612 --> 03:52.739
I'd love some.

03:52.822 --> 03:54.115
How 'bout you, Kahchi?

03:54.198 --> 03:57.452
I make you as a jasmine man.

03:57.535 --> 03:58.619
Am I right?

03:59.162 --> 04:01.539
MONGKE: Enough stalling, round 'em up!

04:03.082 --> 04:04.500
( GRUNTING )

04:19.932 --> 04:21.434
( GRUNTS )

04:25.313 --> 04:26.439
Ah!

04:42.789 --> 04:44.665
It's nice to see old friends.

04:44.749 --> 04:48.002
Too bad you don't have any old friends
that don't want to attack you.

04:48.085 --> 04:49.253
Hmm...

04:49.337 --> 04:52.089
Old friends that don't want to attack me?

05:00.723 --> 05:03.476
( PANTING )

05:04.519 --> 05:05.520
Unh.

05:05.603 --> 05:07.104
Can't you watch where you're...

05:07.188 --> 05:09.315
- No.
- Right, sorry.

05:09.732 --> 05:11.776
Come on, guys, we've gotta stick together.

05:12.151 --> 05:15.571
If I sweat anymore, I don't think
stickin' together will be a problem.

05:15.822 --> 05:18.032
Katara, can I have some water?

05:18.407 --> 05:21.369
Okay, but we've gotta try to conserve it.

05:25.581 --> 05:28.292
We're drinking your bending water?

05:28.417 --> 05:30.127
( SMACKS LIPS )

05:30.211 --> 05:32.338
You used this on the swamp guy!

05:32.421 --> 05:34.549
- Ugh!
- It does taste swampy.

05:34.841 --> 05:36.843
( SMACKING LIPS, BURPS )

05:36.968 --> 05:39.136
I'm sorry, it's all we have.

05:39.387 --> 05:41.013
Not anymore, look.

05:45.309 --> 05:48.229
Sokka, wait, you shouldn't
be eating strange plants.

05:48.437 --> 05:50.189
( GULPING ) Ahh...

05:50.815 --> 05:52.608
There's water trapped inside these.

05:52.692 --> 05:54.902
- I don't know.
- Suit yourself.

05:54.986 --> 05:56.779
It's very thirst-quenching, though.

06:02.827 --> 06:04.495
( VOICE ECHOING ) Drink cactus juice.

06:04.579 --> 06:05.830
It'll quench you.

06:06.038 --> 06:07.748
Nothing's quenchier.

06:07.832 --> 06:09.750
It's the quenchiest!

06:10.209 --> 06:12.295
Okay, I think you've had enough.

06:13.212 --> 06:15.006
Who lit Toph on fire?

06:15.464 --> 06:17.425
( PURRING )

06:17.508 --> 06:18.634
Unh!

06:18.801 --> 06:20.261
Can I get some of that cactus?

06:20.344 --> 06:21.971
I don't think that's a good idea.

06:22.054 --> 06:23.931
Come on, we need to find Aang.

06:27.226 --> 06:30.730
SOKKA: How did we get out here
in the middle of the ocean?

06:30.813 --> 06:31.814
KATARA: ( SIGHS )

06:41.365 --> 06:42.909
Appa!

06:48.039 --> 06:50.625
Appa!

06:56.964 --> 06:58.591
No...

07:00.551 --> 07:02.553
No!

07:10.645 --> 07:11.896
What is that?

07:11.979 --> 07:13.147
What, what is what?

07:13.230 --> 07:16.484
SOKKA: It's a giant mushroom.

07:16.734 --> 07:18.694
Maybe it's friendly!

07:19.111 --> 07:20.279
Let's just keep moving.

07:20.446 --> 07:21.656
I hope Aang's okay...

07:21.906 --> 07:23.616
( VOICE ECHOING ) Friendly mushroom!

07:23.699 --> 07:26.786
Mushy, giant friend!

07:29.747 --> 07:32.166
Yeah, a little, barefoot blind girl

07:32.249 --> 07:34.835
and her friends passed through here
a few days ago.

07:35.044 --> 07:37.964
Did they give you any indication
where they were headed?

07:38.965 --> 07:41.592
Maybe you could give me
a little incentive?

07:42.093 --> 07:45.262
You suggesting I break your fingers?

07:45.513 --> 07:47.056
They went in the desert.

07:47.139 --> 07:49.850
Too bad there's almost no chance
they survived.

07:50.184 --> 07:53.771
Mmm, that's okay,
'cause she's wanted dead or alive.

07:53.980 --> 07:55.398
No, she's not.

07:55.481 --> 07:57.942
I'm certain her father wants her alive.

07:58.567 --> 07:59.610
Hey, look.

07:59.735 --> 08:02.405
Fire Nation wanted posters.

08:02.488 --> 08:03.531
So?

08:03.990 --> 08:06.951
So, look who's here.

08:25.886 --> 08:27.179
KATARA: I'm sorry, Aang.

08:27.304 --> 08:31.142
I know it's hard for you right now, but
we need to focus on getting out of here.

08:31.225 --> 08:32.309
What's the difference?

08:32.852 --> 08:34.353
We won't survive without Appa.

08:34.437 --> 08:35.604
We all know it.

08:35.855 --> 08:36.981
Come on, Aang.

08:37.064 --> 08:39.525
We can do this
if we work together, right, Toph?

08:39.859 --> 08:43.863
As far as I can feel, we're trapped
in a giant bowl of sand pudding.

08:44.280 --> 08:45.406
I got nothin'.

08:45.740 --> 08:48.367
Sokka, any ideas how to find Ba Sing Se?

08:48.492 --> 08:51.203
Why don't we ask the circle birds?

09:03.090 --> 09:05.968
-( PURRING )
-( LAUGHING SOFTLY )

09:08.012 --> 09:09.055
Ugh.

09:09.138 --> 09:12.266
We're getting out of this desert,
and we're gonna do it together.

09:12.349 --> 09:13.517
Aang, get up.

09:13.601 --> 09:14.685
Everybody, hold hands.

09:14.769 --> 09:17.772
We can do this. We have to.

09:19.065 --> 09:20.149
( LAUGHING )

09:20.232 --> 09:22.026
( PURRING )

09:25.905 --> 09:29.492
( WINGS BUZZING )

09:38.125 --> 09:39.919
I think we should stop for the night.

09:40.002 --> 09:42.129
ALL: ( GROANING )

09:43.172 --> 09:44.632
Is there any more water?

09:44.840 --> 09:46.300
This is the last of it.

09:46.425 --> 09:48.511
Everyone can have a little drink.

09:50.846 --> 09:54.433
( SCREAMING ) Momo, no,
you've killed us all!

09:54.850 --> 09:56.727
KATARA: No, he hasn't.

09:56.894 --> 10:00.064
Oh, right, bending.

10:02.983 --> 10:05.569
Sokka, let me see the things
you got from the library.

10:05.653 --> 10:07.655
What? I didn't steal anything!

10:07.738 --> 10:08.989
Who told you that?

10:09.323 --> 10:10.366
It was you!

10:10.449 --> 10:13.244
You ratted me out!

10:14.245 --> 10:16.247
Sokka, I was there.

10:18.040 --> 10:19.333
AANG: It doesn't matter.

10:20.042 --> 10:22.253
None of those will tell us where Appa is.

10:22.378 --> 10:25.714
No, but we can find out
which way Ba Sing Se is.

10:26.173 --> 10:28.217
We can use the stars to guide us.

10:28.300 --> 10:31.846
That way, we can travel at night
when it's cool, and rest during the day.

10:32.221 --> 10:33.430
( SIGHS )

10:35.224 --> 10:36.851
Just try to get some sleep.

10:36.934 --> 10:39.562
We'll start again in a few hours.

10:42.690 --> 10:44.150
No one here is gonna help us.

10:44.275 --> 10:46.402
These people just look like
filthy wanderers.

10:46.902 --> 10:48.154
So do we.

10:49.029 --> 10:52.199
Ah, this is interesting.

10:52.741 --> 10:56.078
I think I've found our friend.

10:57.788 --> 11:00.082
You brought us here to gamble on Pai Sho?

11:00.457 --> 11:03.544
I don't think this is a gamble.

11:05.462 --> 11:06.714
Let's take them now.

11:07.006 --> 11:09.592
This place is full of
desperate characters.

11:09.675 --> 11:12.469
If they find out
we're collecting a bounty,

11:12.553 --> 11:15.890
we might have to fight them all,
just to keep our prize.

11:16.140 --> 11:17.725
Patience.

11:19.685 --> 11:21.395
May I have this game?

11:22.271 --> 11:24.982
The guest has the first move.

11:28.319 --> 11:31.322
I see you favor the White Lotus Gambit.

11:31.405 --> 11:33.824
Not many still cling to the ancient ways.

11:34.825 --> 11:38.120
Those who do can always find a friend.

11:38.412 --> 11:40.164
Then let us play.

11:56.222 --> 11:57.598
Welcome, brother.

11:57.765 --> 12:01.602
The White Lotus opens wide
to those who know her secrets.

12:02.144 --> 12:04.855
What are you old gasbags talking about?

12:04.939 --> 12:10.611
I always tried to tell you
that Pai Sho is more than just a game.

12:12.488 --> 12:16.075
I'm not waiting all night
for these geezers to finish yapping!

12:17.534 --> 12:19.286
It's over!

12:19.370 --> 12:21.538
You two fugitives are coming with me.

12:21.664 --> 12:23.207
I knew it!

12:23.582 --> 12:27.002
You two are wanted criminals
with a giant bounty on your heads!

12:27.211 --> 12:28.796
I thought you said he would help.

12:28.879 --> 12:31.173
He is, just watch.

12:31.340 --> 12:34.426
You think you're going to capture them
and collect all that gold?

12:34.593 --> 12:35.886
Gold?

12:41.183 --> 12:43.143
Uh, maybe we shouldn't...

12:47.773 --> 12:49.233
( GRUNTING )

12:50.276 --> 12:51.568
( GRUNTS )

13:04.999 --> 13:06.000
( GRUNTS )

13:06.250 --> 13:08.252
( SCREAMING )

13:12.631 --> 13:14.633
( MOANING )

13:14.717 --> 13:17.094
KATARA: Come on, get up, we need to go.

13:19.972 --> 13:21.015
( SMACKING LIPS )

13:21.515 --> 13:23.976
Yesterday, my mouth tasted like mud.

13:24.393 --> 13:26.061
Now, it just tastes like sand.

13:26.186 --> 13:29.356
I never thought
I'd miss the taste of mud so much.

13:30.024 --> 13:31.066
AANG: I'm awake.

13:31.191 --> 13:32.776
I couldn't sleep.

13:33.527 --> 13:36.947
Well, we need to get moving
if we want to get out of this sand pit.

13:38.824 --> 13:39.825
Appa!

13:39.908 --> 13:40.993
SOKKA: Appa?

13:41.076 --> 13:43.078
But why would Princess Yue need him?

13:43.162 --> 13:46.373
She's the moon, she flies by herself.

13:49.501 --> 13:51.128
It's just a cloud.

13:51.253 --> 13:53.130
Wait, a cloud!

13:53.213 --> 13:57.301
Here, fly up and bend the water
from that cloud into my pouch.

14:14.985 --> 14:16.945
Wow, there's hardly any in here.

14:17.029 --> 14:18.614
AANG: ( SHOUTING ) I'm sorry, okay?

14:18.697 --> 14:20.574
It's a desert cloud, I did all I could.

14:20.657 --> 14:21.867
What's anyone else doing?

14:21.950 --> 14:23.285
What are you doing?

14:24.912 --> 14:26.997
Trying to keep everyone together.

14:27.456 --> 14:28.832
Let's just get moving.

14:28.916 --> 14:30.417
We need to head this direction.

14:33.587 --> 14:35.130
Ow!

14:35.464 --> 14:39.218
Crud, I am so sick of
not feeling where I'm going.

14:39.802 --> 14:42.971
And what idiot buried a boat
in the middle of the desert?

14:43.055 --> 14:44.098
A boat?

14:44.181 --> 14:47.351
Believe me, I kicked it hard enough
to feel plenty of vibrations.

14:47.434 --> 14:48.519
( MOANS )

14:58.445 --> 15:01.115
KATARA: It's one of the gliders
the sandbenders use.

15:01.532 --> 15:03.951
And look, it's got
some kind of compass on it.

15:04.410 --> 15:06.453
I bet it can point us out of here.

15:07.996 --> 15:10.666
Aang, you can bend a breeze
so we can sail it.

15:10.749 --> 15:11.834
We're gonna make it!

15:12.876 --> 15:14.461
( LAUGHING )

15:14.545 --> 15:15.671
( PURRS )

15:24.430 --> 15:26.098
It is an honor to welcome

15:26.181 --> 15:29.184
such a high-ranking member
of the Order of the White Lotus.

15:29.560 --> 15:32.729
Being a grand master,
you must know so many secrets.

15:33.772 --> 15:37.151
Now that you've played Pai Sho,
are you gonna do some flower arranging?

15:37.234 --> 15:39.862
Or is someone in this club
gonna offer some real help?

15:40.195 --> 15:42.281
You must forgive my nephew.

15:42.573 --> 15:48.245
He is not an initiate, and has
little appreciation for the cryptic arts.

15:51.165 --> 15:52.875
Who knocks at the guarded gate?

15:53.083 --> 15:56.753
One who has eaten the fruit
and tasted its mysteries.

16:03.927 --> 16:05.596
I'm afraid it's members only.

16:05.762 --> 16:07.306
Wait out here.

16:11.268 --> 16:12.936
( SNIFFS )

16:21.778 --> 16:25.115
KATARA: The needle on this compass
doesn't seem to be pointing north,

16:25.199 --> 16:26.617
according to my charts.

16:26.992 --> 16:28.911
( DREAMILY ) Take it easy, little lady.

16:28.994 --> 16:33.207
I'm sure the sand folks who built this
baby know how to get around here.

16:33.749 --> 16:34.958
( GASPS )

16:35.083 --> 16:37.377
KATARA: That's what the compass
is pointing to.

16:37.503 --> 16:38.670
That giant rock.

16:38.795 --> 16:40.964
It must be the magnetic center
of the desert.

16:41.048 --> 16:42.299
A rock?

16:42.424 --> 16:43.842
Yes, let's go!

16:43.967 --> 16:45.969
Maybe we can find some water there.

16:46.094 --> 16:48.263
Maybe we can find some sandbenders.

16:58.690 --> 17:01.235
Ah, finally.

17:01.360 --> 17:04.530
Solid ground.

17:08.909 --> 17:10.953
SOKKA: ( BREATHING DEEPLY )

17:11.036 --> 17:13.914
I think my head is starting
to clear out the cactus juice.

17:14.998 --> 17:17.668
And look!

17:17.793 --> 17:20.337
( BOTH SPUTTERING )

17:20.462 --> 17:22.673
Tastes like rotten penguin meat.

17:23.173 --> 17:25.425
Oh, I feel woozy.

17:25.717 --> 17:28.053
You've been hallucinating
on cactus juice all day,

17:28.178 --> 17:32.099
and then you just lick something
you find stuck to the wall of a cave?

17:32.182 --> 17:33.892
I have a natural curiosity.

17:34.601 --> 17:36.478
I don't think this is a normal cave.

17:37.145 --> 17:38.981
This was carved by something.

17:39.273 --> 17:42.234
AANG: Yeah, look at the shape.

17:42.818 --> 17:45.028
TOPH: There's something buzzing in here.

17:45.237 --> 17:46.863
Something that's coming for us!

17:50.826 --> 17:51.868
( SCREAMING )

17:51.952 --> 17:53.203
( WINGS BUZZING )

18:02.504 --> 18:03.630
( INSECT SHRIEKING )

18:08.218 --> 18:09.469
( SCREECHES )

18:11.305 --> 18:12.681
TOPH: ( GRUNTS )

18:13.098 --> 18:14.266
Oh!

18:14.391 --> 18:15.517
What are you doing?

18:15.642 --> 18:17.144
That rock almost crushed me.

18:17.269 --> 18:19.771
Sorry, I can't tell
where they are in the air.

18:19.855 --> 18:20.981
I got this one.

18:21.231 --> 18:23.191
( SCREAMING )

18:23.275 --> 18:25.068
KATARA: Sokka, there's nothing there.

18:25.235 --> 18:26.403
Huh?

18:26.945 --> 18:29.114
I guess my head's not as clear
as I thought.

18:29.197 --> 18:30.866
KATARA: We have to get out of here.

18:30.949 --> 18:32.701
I'm completely out of water to bend.

18:32.784 --> 18:33.869
MOMO: ( SCREECHES )

18:33.952 --> 18:35.120
AANG: Momo!

18:35.621 --> 18:37.664
I'm not losing anyone else out here.

18:41.501 --> 18:43.170
Come on, we're going down.

18:44.504 --> 18:45.964
( INSECT SHRIEKS )

18:46.048 --> 18:47.966
KATARA: Toph, shoot a rock, right there.

18:48.050 --> 18:49.551
Fire!

18:50.052 --> 18:51.219
( SCREECHES )

18:51.345 --> 18:52.763
SOKKA: Yeah, you got it!

18:52.846 --> 18:53.930
She got it, right?

18:54.056 --> 18:56.183
Yes. Now, let's move.

18:59.144 --> 19:00.771
MOMO: ( CHATTERING )

19:06.443 --> 19:07.736
( GRUNTS )

19:09.488 --> 19:10.572
( CHATTERS )

19:18.830 --> 19:20.374
( GRUNTING )

19:32.386 --> 19:33.804
KATARA: On your left.

19:34.054 --> 19:35.722
( INSECT SHRIEKS )

20:01.456 --> 20:03.500
What's going on? Is the club meeting over?

20:03.625 --> 20:05.919
Everything is taken care of.

20:06.461 --> 20:08.672
We're heading to Ba Sing Se.

20:08.880 --> 20:10.298
Ba Sing Se?

20:10.424 --> 20:12.592
Why would we go to
the Earth Kingdom capital?

20:12.676 --> 20:14.594
The city is filled with refugees.

20:14.678 --> 20:16.346
No one will notice two more.

20:16.596 --> 20:18.932
We can hide in plain sight there.

20:19.182 --> 20:22.853
And it's the safest place
in the world from the Fire Nation.

20:23.270 --> 20:25.856
Even I couldn't break through to the city.

20:25.939 --> 20:26.982
( DOOR OPENS )

20:27.065 --> 20:28.817
I have the passports for our guests,

20:28.900 --> 20:31.570
but there are two men
out on the street looking for them.

20:34.406 --> 20:36.616
You seen these guys?

20:38.118 --> 20:41.621
MAN: What are you doing
in our land with a sandbender sailer?

20:41.705 --> 20:45.083
From the looks of it,
you stole it from the Hami tribe.

20:45.292 --> 20:47.461
We found the sailer
abandoned in the desert.

20:47.544 --> 20:49.421
We're traveling with the Avatar.

20:50.046 --> 20:53.467
Our bison was stolen,
and we have to get to Ba Sing Se.

20:53.592 --> 20:55.719
You dare accuse our people of theft,

20:55.802 --> 20:58.180
while you ride in on a stolen sand sailer?

20:58.263 --> 21:00.015
Quiet, Ghashiun!

21:00.098 --> 21:02.476
No one accused our people of anything.

21:02.559 --> 21:05.812
If what they say is true,
we must give them hospitality.

21:06.438 --> 21:07.647
GHASHIUN: Sorry, father.

21:07.981 --> 21:10.358
TOPH: I recognize the son's voice.

21:10.442 --> 21:12.861
He's the one that stole Appa.

21:13.236 --> 21:16.031
- Are you sure?
- TOPH: I never forget a voice.

21:16.490 --> 21:18.366
You stole Appa.

21:18.450 --> 21:20.368
Where is he? What did you do to him?

21:20.452 --> 21:22.788
They're lying. They're the thieves!

21:23.747 --> 21:25.040
( GRUNTING )

21:27.667 --> 21:30.003
Where is my bison?

21:38.887 --> 21:41.264
Hey, you. Where are these men?

21:41.389 --> 21:43.308
I got a tip that they're in your shop.

21:43.809 --> 21:46.853
As you can see, no one is here but us.

21:47.479 --> 21:50.232
We know all about your secret back room.

21:50.482 --> 21:52.526
Kick it down.

21:53.026 --> 21:54.903
Hey, that room is for flowers only.

21:59.866 --> 22:04.454
Some unlucky soul
has an incomplete Pai Sho set.

22:04.788 --> 22:09.376
( GRUNTING )
Let's go back to finding the girl.

22:18.927 --> 22:21.304
You tell me where he is, now!

22:23.640 --> 22:25.100
What did you do?

22:25.183 --> 22:26.476
It wasn't me.

22:26.601 --> 22:28.854
TOPH: You said to put a muzzle on him.

22:28.937 --> 22:31.481
You muzzled Appa?

22:37.779 --> 22:38.822
GHASHIUN: I'm sorry!

22:38.947 --> 22:40.866
I didn't know it belonged to the Avatar!

22:40.949 --> 22:43.159
( IN DISTORTED VOICE )
Tell me where Appa is.

22:43.243 --> 22:45.203
I traded him to some merchants.

22:45.412 --> 22:47.998
He's probably in Ba Sing Se by now.

22:48.081 --> 22:49.958
They were gonna sell him there.

22:50.876 --> 22:53.003
Please, we'll escort you
out of the desert.

22:53.086 --> 22:54.546
We'll help however we can.

22:56.882 --> 22:59.801
SOKKA: Just get out of here, run!

23:47.807 --> 23:52.228
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
